From f32342a650caea4c2449bbf0f9e6fcf3da8fee99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:17:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the help of four settings names the program that
 runs Hades, not Kodi

The build shows itself as LibreELEC Hades, and the help of its settings says "Hades" for
what the program does. Four texts new in this version said "Kodi" there: "Colour format"
(where the driver lets Kodi choose it), "Maximum bit depth" (where Kodi can set it), "HDR
in 4:2:2 at 12 bits over HDMI 2.0" (what Kodi draws over the video) and "Keep the graphics
card at full speed while HD audio plays through" (without Kodi decoding it, or Kodi
closes), in English (core 41311, 41318, 41401, 41851 and their Estuary twins 32911,
32918, 33001, 32951) and in es_es, es_ar and es_mx.

They say "Hades". "Kodi" stays where it is the reference that Hades is compared with ("as
in Kodi", "as Kodi plays it") and in kodi.log.

Host test (outside the tree): kodiname.py reads every text of these five files that is
new or changed since the base of this version: before, 20 of them name the program
Kodi; after, none. The core and Estuary texts are still the same (maptest.py), and so is
the English that each Spanish file translates (msgidsync.py).
