@@ -27314,7 +27314,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadescolorformat"; translated in Estuary (#32911)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#41311"
-msgid "The colour format that the graphics card sends to the display, where the driver lets Kodi choose it (AMD graphics, and NVIDIA graphics with driver 620 on HDMI, which has no 4:2:0). Automatic is what LibreELEC Hades does without this setting. A format that the driver cannot carry in a mode (for example YCbCr 4:4:4 at 3840x2160 and 60 Hz over HDMI 2.0) goes out as Automatic in that mode, and the log says so. Dolby Vision always goes out as RGB at 8 bits. Applies with the next change of mode, or the next video that signals HDR."
